    "ungraded": false,
    "solution": "1. 4x + 6y + 2z — Multiply each quantity by its unit price, then add.\n2. -8 — The signed multiplier of p is −8.\n3. −12x + 8 — Multiply both 3x and −2 by −4.\n4. 6a + 12b − 18 — Distribute 6 to all three terms.\n5. −12a²b — Multiply coefficients and both factors of a.\n6. 6y² − 8xy — Multiply 2y by each term.\n7. 2x + 4y — 6x + 3y − 4x + y = 2x + 4y.\n8. 5ab and −2ba — ab and ba represent the same variable product.\n9. 7 — −6 + 8 + 5 = 7.\n10. 13 — 2(8) − 3 = 13.",
    "solution_reveal": "NEVER"
  },
